00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:23.266
survey of consumer expectations, and the decision it supports is a sector tilt.

00:02:23.266 --> 00:02:26.606
Note, not a single name gamble before the next rate announcement.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:31.766
You pull the latest PDF off the Bank of Canada site, write down the net percentage of

00:02:31.766 --> 00:02:34.646
firms expecting stronger sales or tighter labor markets.

00:02:35.186 --> 00:02:39.686
Then in your brokerage screener, you line those readings up against TSX Sector Exchange

00:02:39.686 --> 00:02:44.966
Traded Fund, or ETF Holdings and favor the groups that historically moved when those

00:02:44.966 --> 00:02:49.386
nets improved, which in prior cycles meant industrials and consumer names.

00:02:49.386 --> 00:02:49.546
teams.

00:02:50.186 --> 00:02:54.506
Think of it like tasting every pot in a cafeteria whose menu was built to match the

00:02:54.506 --> 00:02:55.266
city's appetite.

00:02:55.866 --> 00:02:58.386
You are not asking your favorite cook how lunch will go.

00:02:58.866 --> 00:03:02.366
You are sampling the same mix of kitchens the economy actually runs on.

00:03:02.966 --> 00:03:07.286
What would you do if the net expecting stronger sales jumped and industrials looked cheap

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:08.586
on the T-SX screen?

00:03:09.166 --> 00:03:13.586
Overweight the sector inside a T-F-S-A or wait for the rate decision itself.

00:03:14.206 --> 00:03:18.946
I treat the survey as a confirmation layer, not a standalone trigger, because the same

00:03:18.946 --> 00:03:23.926
Some approach failed when geopolitical shocks overrode the domestic signal, and because survey

00:03:23.926 --> 00:03:26.066
answers lag sudden external events.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:31.986
Combine the response mix across regions and firm sizes with those ETF screens so you

00:03:31.986 --> 00:03:36.906
are allocating to revenue exposure that already lines up with improving sentiment, which is

00:03:36.906 --> 00:03:38.806
how you stop chasing overnight headlines.

00:03:39.426 --> 00:03:42.786
